cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ActivityPlan"
abstract: "Onboard activity planning with an auditable timeline — declared activities (duration, power profile, data produced, priority, windows, precedence, exclusions) against a declared resource model (battery capacity and depth-of-discharge limit, solar input, recorder capacity, contact windows and rates); greedy earliest-feasible-start and exact MILP baselines, a learned duration/energy predictor with calibrated prediction intervals used to warm-start the solver and to build a robust plan, scored against the exact optimum on optimality gap and solve time, and a feasibility report naming the binding constraint and the slack on every other one."
type: software
